## Bug report from the product owner (iPhone 12, iOS 26.6, internal build 4 with today's OTA)
"The alarm immediately moves to overdue status the moment I don't attend to it. This is when the phone is open or closed. It remains in that state even after I tap Later (delay/reschedule). Only after some time does the state update to show when it should next ring. I want to change that: while it is ringing we don't update the card's state; only after ringing ends — timeout, Done, or Later/reschedule — do we change state. Also, when the phone is unlocked and I tap the X on the alarm notification that pops up, the card shows overdue. Can we replace that X with a tick (Done) instead, and clear the alarm once we clear it?"

## Where to start (anchors, not a map)
- Card state text and ordering: `lib/remindersMembership.ts`, `lib/time.ts` (`formatNextIn`), `components/ReminderListItem.tsx`, the next-ring resolver (`getReminderNextDueTimestamp`, snooze → `nextGridOccurrence` → legacy, per the 09-08 devlog `updates/2026-09-08_devlog.md:22-35`), refresh cadence (30 s tick + AppState active).
- Ringing: iOS 26 AlarmKit path in `plugins/withAlarmKit.js` (generated Swift, alert presentation ~`:413`), `plugins/ios-src/VRAlarmIntents.swift` (Stop/Snooze App Intents, snooze-guard races), `lib/alarmKit.ts`, the JS-side alarm surfaces `components/AlarmOverlay.tsx` and `app/alarm.tsx`, notifee/notification fallback in `lib/notifications.ts` (`scheduleReminder`, ring planning ~`:2132-2148`, snooze/`Later` handling, `persistent` nag repeats), `docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md`, `docs/alarmkit-test-plan.md`. Snooze state on the reminder row (`lib/store.ts`: fields like snoozedUntil / lastRing / completedAt — find the real names) and how the store learns that a ring ended (Stop/Snooze intents → app? Darwin notification? next-launch reconcile?).
- Which "X" the owner means: the AlarmKit alert has its own buttons (Stop = the X-style dismiss? and Snooze = Later); a notifee/foreground banner may have different actions. Identify exactly which surface shows an X and what it maps to.

## Questions to answer in (3), the interaction matrix
For each: what the user sees on the card during and after, and what state the app has. Rows: (a) phone locked, AlarmKit alert rings, user taps Stop; (b) taps Snooze/Later; (c) ignores it until the alert times out (what is the timeout? does AlarmKit auto-snooze, auto-stop, or keep ringing?); (d) phone unlocked, app in foreground when it rings (which surface shows — AlarmKit alert, AlarmOverlay, banner?); (e) app killed/backgrounded, phone unlocked; (f) Focus / Do Not Disturb on (AlarmKit breaks through? notifee fallback doesn't?); (g) silent switch / volume 0; (h) Low Power Mode; (i) notification permission revoked or alarm authorization denied (fallback path); (j) a repeating/persistent reminder vs a one-off; (k) the user opens the app WHILE it is ringing and taps the card; (l) the user taps Done on the card while it is ringing.

## Claude's initial reasoning for the fix (grill it)
- The card derives "Overdue" purely from `now > nextRing` with no notion of "currently ringing". Proposed: a ringing window — from the scheduled trigger until the ring resolves (Stop/Done, Snooze, or a max ring duration, e.g. AlarmKit's own timeout or a fixed 60-120 s for the fallback) — during which the card keeps showing the pre-ring state ("Now" / "Ringing"), not "Overdue". Persist the resolution (`lastRingResolvedAt`, outcome) on the reminder so a relaunch computes the same thing.
- Snooze must write the new next-ring time to the store synchronously in the same handler that arms the snooze, and trigger the list refresh — not wait for the 30 s tick. If the Snooze happens in the AlarmKit intent (extension/system process) while the app is suspended, the app must reconcile on next foreground from a persisted source (App Group / UserDefaults / the AlarmKit alarm's state) — find what exists.
- The X → tick: if the surface is AlarmKit's system alert, Apple defines the button set (Stop + optional secondary); we can relabel/re-icon Stop as Done with a checkmark if the API allows (check `AlarmButton` in the generated Swift), and Stop should mark the reminder done (one-off) or advance it (repeater), not leave it "overdue". If it is our own in-app overlay/banner, we own it fully.
- "Timed out" ring (ignored): after the window, it IS overdue — that's the honest state — but the card should say "Missed · 3:52 pm" rather than an alarming red the instant the ring starts.
- What should NOT change: the nag/persistent semantics (CL-4 decision: no escalation, snooze-nag instead), the OLD-110/111 lock-screen Done-without-Face-ID behavior, the AlarmKit sound pipeline.

