docs/alarm-banner-research.md:12:
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:13:**A fully custom alarm banner is impossible on a locked phone.** The alerting UI is drawn by the system,
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:14:out of process, from a fixed template. Our entire design surface at fire time is: **one title string, one
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:15:tint color, and one optional secondary button (text + SF Symbol + text color)** â€” and as of **iOS 26.1 even
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:16:the stop button is no longer ours** (`stopButton` is deprecated and ignored; the system renders its own
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:17:slideâ€‘toâ€‘stop control). There is no layout, no image, no body text, no background, no font, no custom view.
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:18:The only surface where we can draw real SwiftUI is the **Live Activity** (Lock Screen banner + Dynamic
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:19:Island + StandBy) â€” and by Apple's own sample docs the widget extension customizes **nonâ€‘alerting**
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:20:presentations only, i.e. countdown and paused, which our app does not currently use at all. When the app is
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:21:**open**, we still do not own the screen: the system alert presents over the foreground app; the only way to
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:22:own the pixels is to observe `AlarmManager.alarmUpdates`, call `stop(id:)` the moment a rung goes
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:23:`.alerting`, and immediately drive our own React Native screen + audio. That native path is not built yet.
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:24:
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:25:---
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:26:
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:27:## Capability matrix
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:28:
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:29:Legend: **Custom** = we set it Â· **Fixed** = system renders, we cannot influence Â· **Impossible** = no API exists.
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:30:
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:31:### A. Locked phone, alarm firing (the fullâ€‘screen alert)
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:32:
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:33:| Element | Status | Detail / citation |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:34:|---|---|---|
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:35:| Title text | **Custom** | `AlarmPresentation.Alert.title: LocalizedStringResource` â€” "The title of the alert." ([docs](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/alarmkit/alarmpresentation/alert-swift.struct)) |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:36:| Title styling (font, size, weight, alignment) | **Fixed** | No API. Only the tint color touches it. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:37:| App name shown under/next to title | **Fixed** | WWDC25 230: "people are presented with the custom alarm title, as well as the name of your app" ([session](https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/230/)) |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:38:| Subtitle / body / second line | **Impossible** | `Alert` has exactly 4 members: `title`, `stopButton`, `secondaryButton`, `secondaryButtonBehavior`. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:39:| Image / artwork / avatar / album art | **Impossible** | No image member anywhere in `AlarmPresentation` or `AlarmAttributes`. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:40:| Background color / material / blur | **Impossible** | Not exposed. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:41:| Tint color | **Custom (narrow)** | `AlarmAttributes.tintColor: Color` â€” "The tint color applied to the templated UI." WWDC25: "On the lock screen, it is used to tint the symbol in the secondary button as well as the alarm title and the countdown." So: secondaryâ€‘button glyph + title text, nothing else. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:42:| **Stop button** label / icon / color | **Fixed on iOS 26.1+** | `stopButton` is **deprecated**: "This property is not used anymore and will be removed." The replacement init is `init(title:secondaryButton:secondaryButtonBehavior:)`, availability **iOS 26.1**, abstract: "Creates an alert for an alarm, **with a system-provided stop control**". iOS 26.1 shipped slideâ€‘toâ€‘stop systemâ€‘wide (users can revert to a tap button via Accessibility â†’ Prefer Singleâ€‘Touch Actions). ([stopButton](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/alarmkit/alarmpresentation/alert-swift.struct/stopbutton), [9to5Mac](https://9to5mac.com/2025/12/11/ios-26-1-makes-alarms-use-a-slider-heres-how-to-get-stop-button-back/)) |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:43:| Stop **action** | **Custom** | `stopIntent:` on `AlarmConfiguration` still runs our App Intent. The label is theirs; the behavior is ours. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:44:| Secondary button â€” presence | **Custom** | `secondaryButton: AlarmButton?` â€” optional. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:45:| Secondary button â€” text | **Custom** | `AlarmButton.text` |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:46:| Secondary button â€” icon | **Custom, SF Symbols only** | `AlarmButton.systemImageName` â€” "The name of the icon you use on the button." No custom/bundled assets. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:47:| Secondary button â€” text color | **Custom** | `AlarmButton.textColor` |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:48:| Secondary button â€” shape/position/size | **Fixed** | Template. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:49:| Third button | **Impossible** | Max two: "each alert displaying up to two buttons". |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:50:| Secondary behavior | **Custom (2 options)** | `.countdown` or `.custom`. No `.snooze` case exists. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:51:| Number of buttons/layout/orientation | **Fixed** | Template. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:52:| Whether it breaks Silent/Focus | **Fixed (always yes)** | WWDC25: "the alert breaks through the silent mode and the current focus." |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:53:| Sound | **Custom (constrained)** | `.default` or `.named(String)` from bundle / `Library/Sounds`; loops until stopped; baked at schedule time. See `cl4-escalation-research.md`. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:54:| Haptics | **Fixed** | No API. |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:55:| Ring duration / autoâ€‘stop | **Impossible** | No API stops an unattended alert (already established in CLâ€‘4 research). |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:56:| **A custom SwiftUI view instead of the alert** | **Impossible** | Sample doc: "The widget extension customizes **non-alerting** presentations in the Dynamic Island, Lock Screen, and StandBy." ([Scheduling an alarm with AlarmKit](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/alarmkit/scheduling-an-alarm-with-alarmkit)) |
docs/alarm-banner-research.md:57:
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:195:| | Mutate a scheduled alarm's sound, title, or time in place | no update API â€” cancel + re-`schedule` with a new id |
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:196:| | Control loop count, ring duration, or fade | no parameter on any type |
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:197:
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:198:## 6. Our integration's unused capabilities
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:199:
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:200:Read against `plugins/withAlarmKit.js` and `lib/alarmKit.ts`. We currently use:
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:201:`requestAuthorization()`, `schedule(id:configuration:)`, `cancel(id:)`, `.fixed(Date)` schedules,
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:202:`AlarmAttributes` (tint + custom `VRAlarmMetadata`), `AlarmPresentation.Alert` with the 26.1 fork,
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:203:`AlertSound.default/.named`, two `LiveActivityIntent`s with `secondaryButtonBehavior: .custom`,
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:204:and the Info.plist key. Everything below is documented and unused:
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:205:
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:206:1. **`alarmUpdates`** â€” "Use this to receive a notification when an alarm alerts, snoozes, or
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:207:   dismisses" ([alarmUpdates](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/alarmkit/alarmmanager/alarmupdates-swift.property)).
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:208:   This is the observer CL-4 option 1 needs, and it is also the only in-process signal that a
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:209:   rung reached `.alerting`. Not wired at all today.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:210:2. **`alarms`** â€” the fix for our dead "fired" event, straight from Apple: "As soon as an alarm
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:211:   fires and stops it's deleted from the daemon's store. If you want to determine if a one-shot
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:212:   alarm has fired, persist your alarms in your own store and compare that with the result of this
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:213:   function call. **If the array is missing scheduled alarms, then those alarms fired.**"
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:214:   ([alarms](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/alarmkit/alarmmanager/alarms)). We already
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:215:   persist a registry (`VRAlarmStore`) â€” the diff is a few lines and needs no fire-time code.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:216:   Today `getScheduledAlarms()` reads our own UserDefaults registry, not the daemon.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:217:3. **`authorizationState` / `authorizationUpdates`** â€” non-prompting reads. Our `useAlarmKit()`
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:218:   gate calls `requestAuthorization()` and caches the answer for the session, so a mid-session
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:219:   revoke in Settings is invisible until relaunch.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:220:4. **`stop(id:)`, `countdown(id:)`, `pause(id:)`, `resume(id:)`** â€” never called. `stop(id:)` is
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:221:   the foreground stop-and-replace primitive.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:222:5. **`countdownDuration` (`preAlert`/`postAlert`)** â€” never set, so the system snooze path
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:223:   (`secondaryButtonBehavior: .countdown` + `postAlert`) is unavailable and our "Later" is a hand-
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:224:   rolled intent + re-registration. Adopting it would require a widget extension.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:225:6. **`.relative` weekly schedules** â€” we re-register a `.fixed` alarm per occurrence. Recurring
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:226:   reminders could be one daemon-side alarm instead of N registrations against the alarm cap.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:227:7. **Widget extension / Live Activity** â€” we ship none, so no custom Lock Screen, Dynamic Island,
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:228:   or StandBy surface, and no countdown UI. Templated presentation only.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:229:8. **`AlarmError.maximumLimitReached`** â€” unhandled. Our cadence ladder registers up to 3 alarms
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:230:   per occurrence, which multiplies our exposure to an undocumented cap.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:231:9. **`appEntityIdentifier` (iOS 27 beta)** â€” would let Siri snooze/dismiss a ringing VoiceReminder
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:232:   alarm hands-free. Genuinely relevant for an accessibility-shaped app; worth an early adopt.
docs/alarmkit-focus-breakthrough.md:233:

