codex
Two important corrections to the proposed fix: iOS 26.1+ owns the AlarmKit stop control, so changing our existing checkmark configuration won’t replace its X. Also, the app’s three-minute “missed” threshold does not control AlarmKit’s ringing duration. The integration currently reads its own saved alarm registry, without observing whether the system alarm is actually alerting.

