docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:1:# CL-4 Research â€” AlarmKit escalation on iOS 26 (2026-08-11)
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:2:
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:3:What the native bridge actually does, what Apple's API allows, and the recommended
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:4:stop-and-replace design. Produced after the device report "alarm repeats the same line,
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:5:no escalation." Tracking: OLD-53.
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:6:
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:7:## How our alarms behave unattended (evidence)
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:8:
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:9:- Bridge config is `VRAlarmScheduler.makeConfiguration` (`plugins/withAlarmKit.js:401-439`):
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:10:  alert-only presentation, no countdown/postAlert anywhere, sound baked at schedule time via
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:11:  `AlertConfiguration.AlertSound.named(...)`. Buttons: Done (stop intent) / Later (snooze intent).
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:12:- **Nothing bounds a ring.** iOS 26.1+ loops the sound file until slide-to-stop. Our WAVs are
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:13:  `[spoken line][silence]` padded to 28s (`convex/helpers.ts` ALARM_WAV_TARGET_SECONDS) â€” so an
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:14:  unattended rung sounds like: line, ~20s silence, same line, forever. That is ONE rung looping,
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:15:  not a failed ladder. Rung 0 owns the first 3 minutes by design (LADDER_OFFSETS_MS = 0/3min/7min,
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:16:  `lib/notificationDecisions.ts:394`).
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:17:- `ALARM_RING_TIMEOUT_MS = 180_000` (`lib/alarmKit.ts:65`) enforces nothing on-device â€” it only
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:18:  classifies drained events on next foreground.
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:19:- **Bug found:** native never appends a "fired" event (Swift emits only stopped/snoozed/
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:20:  sibling_cancelled/snooze_failed), so the missed-classification and missedâ†’follow-up path
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:21:  (`lib/notifications.ts:1800-1842`) are unreachable for AlarmKit alarms. An urgent alarm that
docs/cl4-escalation-research.md:22:  rings out leaves no history entry.
